{"name":"Beauport Aubergine","hex":"#553f44","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aubergine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Asian plant, Solanum melongena, cultivated for its edible purple, green, or white ovoid fruit; eggplant.","The fruit of this plant, eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aubergine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eggplant","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum melongena is a plant species in the nightshade family Solanaceae, grown worldwide for its edible fruit, typically used as a vegetable in cooking. It is known by a number of names, including eggplant, aubergine, and brinjal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG/330px-Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant","wikidata":"Q7540"},{"title":"Eggplant (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Eggplant is a dark purple or brownish-purple color that resembles the color of the outer skin of European eggplants. Another name for the color eggplant is aubergine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Aubergine.jpg/330px-Aubergine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant_(color)","wikidata":"Q1403218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/1280px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wi